course: dictionary
lesson: 798
title: One word, two meanings: beet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean different things in different places, so use the words around it to find which meaning fits. A beet is a round, dark red vegetable that grows under the ground. In the UK it is called beetroot.
explain: «Sugar comes from sugar cane or sugar beet.» Here beet is not the dark red vegetable. The clues are sugar and comes from: sugar beet is a pale kind of beet that sugar is made from.
explain: Beet also appears in a saying, «red as a beet». Nobody means a vegetable here. The clue is red in the face, so it means very red in the face, from shame or heat. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A beet is a root: it stores food for the plant, so the part we eat grows under the ground.
fact: Beets turn food and fingers red when you cook or chop them.
fact: Sugar beet is a pale kind of beet, and sugar is made from it.
fact: Most sugar made in Britain comes from sugar beet, which grows in cool countries where sugar cane cannot.
fact: «Red as a beet» means very red in the face, from shame or heat.
exercise: «Most sugar made in Britain comes from sugar beet, a pale root that grows in cool countries.» What is sugar beet? | A dark red vegetable you eat cold in salads | A tall grass taller than a grown-up | A kind of cake | *A pale kind of beet that sugar is made from
exercise: After Sam chopped the beets, his fingers were bright red. Why? | *Beets turn food and fingers red | Sam had been running in the sun | Beets are a kind of sugar | Beets are always cold
exercise: Maria says her face went «red as a beet» after she dropped the cake. What does this mean? | Pale and cold | Covered in sugar | *Very red in the face, from shame or heat | Hungry for dinner
test: In «The beet is a root that stores food for the plant», where does the beet store its food? | *In its root, under the ground | In a sugar cane | In its petals | In the sky
test: Which word names the pale root that sugar is made from? | Red beet salad | *Sugar beet | Sugar cane | Beetroot
exam: Which is the best meaning of beet in «Sugar comes from sugar cane or sugar beet»? | A sweet cake | A tall grass like a giant | *A pale root that sugar is made from | A dark red vegetable for salads
